      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 3.09,
          "en": "So now we got started",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.09,
          "end": 6.06,
          "en": "creating this Expense class and we're almost done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.06,
          "end": 9.54,
          "en": "But there's actually one piece of information missing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.54,
          "end": 12.81,
          "en": "that should also belong to Expense objects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.81,
          "end": 16.65,
          "en": "and that's the category to which an expense belongs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.65,
          "end": 19.23,
          "en": "Because in this finished app, which we're building,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.23,
          "end": 22.65,
          "en": "every expense has a category attached to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.65,
          "end": 26.76,
          "en": "which is important for that chart that will be built,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.76,
          "end": 30.63,
          "en": "because that chart groups expenses by category.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.63,
          "end": 33.6,
          "en": "So therefore here I also wanna store some category",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.6,
          "end": 36.153,
          "en": "information in my expense class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.08,
          "end": 38.43,
          "en": "And you could now of course say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.43,
          "end": 41.04,
          "en": "that you wanna to have a category property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.04,
          "end": 43.08,
          "en": "which is of type String.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.08,
          "end": 47.7,
          "en": "This would allow us to add categories as string values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.7,
          "end": 50.73,
          "en": "to these expenses as we create them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.73,
          "end": 53.52,
          "en": "But this could be quite error prone,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.52,
          "end": 54.9,
          "en": "because if you, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.9,
          "end": 59.67,
          "en": "wanna support the category leisure like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.67,
          "end": 62.82,
          "en": "we could of course create such a Expense object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.82,
          "end": 65.52,
          "en": "by calling Expense and passing leisure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.52,
          "end": 68.34,
          "en": "like this as a category value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.34,
          "end": 69.39,
          "en": "But it could happen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.39,
          "end": 72.36,
          "en": "that we accidentally introduce a typo here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.36,
          "end": 76.23,
          "en": "and we wouldn't get any warning or error when doing so,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.23,
          "end": 79.23,
          "en": "because any kind of string value is accepted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.23,
          "end": 80.88,
          "en": "So even though that might not be one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.88,
          "end": 83.31,
          "en": "of the categories we wanna support to this app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.31,
          "end": 87.93,
          "en": "we wouldn't get an error, because it is a valid string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.93,
          "end": 90.45,
          "en": "It just wouldn't show up in our chart,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.45,
          "end": 94.05,
          "en": "because there we might not look for this category",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.05,
          "end": 95.643,
          "en": "because it contains a typo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.63,
          "end": 99.53999999999999,
          "en": "So for that reason, using a string here is not optimal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.53999999999999,
          "end": 104.07,
          "en": "It's too flexible, it allows too many values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.07,
          "end": 107.88,
          "en": "Instead, we wanna create a fixed set of allowed values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.88,
          "end": 110.78999999999999,
          "en": "so that we have to use one of those values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 110.78999999999999,
          "end": 113.25,
          "en": "when creating a new expense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.25,
          "end": 115.8,
          "en": "And for that, we can create a new value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.8,
          "end": 118.97999999999999,
          "en": "that contains all these allowed values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.97999999999999,
          "end": 121.17,
          "en": "with another special Dart feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.17,
          "end": 124.32300000000001,
          "en": "the enum feature, the enum keyword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.618,
          "end": 129.09,
          "en": "enum is a keyword that allows us to create a custom type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129.09,
          "end": 132.03,
          "en": "You could say that could be named Category here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 132.03,
          "end": 137.03,
          "en": "which simply is a combination of predefined allowed values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 138.32999999999998,
          "end": 140.52,
          "en": "You define those allowed values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 140.52,
          "end": 142.98,
          "en": "between opening and closing curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.98,
          "end": 147.03,
          "en": "So this simply is the enum syntax in Dart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147.03,
          "end": 147.863,
          "en": "And then here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.863,
          "end": 150.72,
          "en": "between those opening and closing curly braces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 150.72,
          "end": 154.02,
          "en": "you list your enum values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 154.02,
          "end": 157.05,
          "en": "For example, here, for the Expense categories",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 157.05,
          "end": 159.18,
          "en": "that we wanna support in this app here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 159.18,
          "end": 164.18,
          "en": "I wanna have food, travel, leisure, and work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 164.30700000000002,
          "end": 166.82999999999998,
          "en": "And of course you could add more though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 166.82999999999998,
          "end": 169.5,
          "en": "These will be the categories I will later output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 169.5,
          "end": 170.403,
          "en": "in my chart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 171.87,
          "end": 175.17000000000002,
          "en": "So with that, we're simply saying that in this project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 175.17000000000002,
          "end": 177.54,
          "en": "in this Dart project, in this app here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 177.54,
          "end": 180.69,
          "en": "we wanna have a custom type category",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 180.69,
          "end": 184.17,
          "en": "that supports these possible values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 184.17,
          "end": 188.4,
          "en": "Please note that these values are not wrapped in quotes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 188.4,
          "end": 191.58,
          "en": "So we don't have string values here technically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 191.58,
          "end": 192.6,
          "en": "but nonetheless,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 192.6,
          "end": 195.45,
          "en": "this entire syntax here is recognized by Dart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 195.45,
          "end": 200.19,
          "en": "and treats these values kind of like string values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 200.19,
          "end": 201.93,
          "en": "You will see how we can access them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 201.93,
          "end": 204.483,
          "en": "as text later on in this section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 205.44,
          "end": 207.81,
          "en": "But now with that, we can use Category",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 207.81,
          "end": 211.11,
          "en": "as a custom type here for this category value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 211.11,
          "end": 212.763,
          "en": "in our Expense class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 213.69,
          "end": 217.56,
          "en": "And now of course, we also wanna accept categories",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 217.56,
          "end": 219.12,
          "en": "as input values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 219.12,
          "end": 224.12,
          "en": "And for this here, I will also accept a category parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 224.19,
          "end": 227.643,
          "en": "a named category parameter, which is required.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 228.9,
          "end": 232.92000000000002,
          "en": "And that's now the finished Expense model for the moment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 232.92000000000002,
          "end": 236.52,
          "en": "We'll fine tune and change it a little bit later,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 236.52,
          "end": 238.44,
          "en": "but that's the model for the moment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 238.44,
          "end": 241.44,
          "en": "And with that model defined, we can now switch back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 241.44,
          "end": 245.7,
          "en": "to the UI and make sure that we use that model there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 245.7,
          "end": 248.583,
          "en": "And for example, output a list of expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
